 The route#b function takes the request path and traverses the specified domain hierarchy along its matching fields. Functional values are invoked with the current route scope, the original request and its body ((route)#script/highlight(`value.call(this,request,body)`){display:inline;white-space:normal;word-break:break-all;white-space:normal}), and traversal continues on their returned values. A "folder" path with a trailing slash is appended a default route for html representations (.../interface). The "method" field on HTTP requests can be considered an alternative route for when the path would lead to a dead end ((route)#script/highlight(`scope[method].call(this,request,body)`){display:inline;white-space:normal;word-break:break-all;white-space:normal}), but only once as branch#b records this invocation. To associate certain routes with arbitrary scopes, a third fallback rebinds the scope to origin routes (/author/name/interface -> route#script/highlight(`domain.interface.call(author,request,body)`){display:inline;white-space:normal;word-break:break-all;white-space:normal}. 

